---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { legal, site } from '../site.config';

// Privacy policy template according to the GDPR (DSGVO) and the Austrian
// Datenschutzgesetz (DSG). It describes exactly what this website does:
// no cookies, no analytics, no external fonts or embeds, a contact form sent by email.
// If you add anything (analytics, maps, embedded Instagram), update this page first.
// This is a template, not legal advice. Have it reviewed.
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy" description={`Privacy policy of ${site.name}.`} noindex>
  <section class="section container narrow prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>
      Protecting your personal data is important to us. This policy explains which data we
      process when you visit this website or contact us, and what rights you have under the
      General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and the Austrian Data Protection Act (DSG).
    </p>

    <h2>1. Controller</h2>
    <p>
      {legal.ownerName}<br />
      {legal.street}, {legal.postalCode} {legal.city}, {legal.country}<br />
      Email: <a href={`mailto:${legal.email}`}>{legal.email}</a>
    </p>

    <h2>2. Hosting and server log files</h2>
    <p>
      This website is hosted by Hostinger. {/* TODO: add the exact Hostinger contracting entity and address from your invoice or contract */}
      When you visit the website, the web server automatically stores technical information that
      your browser transmits: IP address, date and time of the request, the requested page,
      referrer URL, browser and operating system.
    </p>
    <p>
      We need this data to deliver the website securely and to detect and defend against attacks.
      The legal basis is our legitimate interest in a secure and working website (Art. 6(1)(f)
      GDPR). The log files are stored by the hosting provider for a limited period and then
      deleted automatically. We have concluded a data processing agreement with the hosting
      provider (Art. 28 GDPR). The data is processed on servers within the European Union.
      {/* TODO: confirm the data centre location chosen in hPanel */}
    </p>

    <h2>3. Cookies, analytics and external services</h2>
    <p>
      This website does not use cookies, tracking or analytics tools. Fonts are served from our
      own server, so no connection to Google or other font providers is made. No content from
      social networks or map services is embedded.
    </p>
    <p>
      The footer contains a plain link to our Instagram profile. Data is only transferred to
      Instagram (Meta Platforms Ireland Ltd.) if you click on this link and leave our website.
      The privacy policy of Instagram then applies.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Contact form and email</h2>
    <p>
      If you contact us through the contact form or by email, we process the data you provide:
      name, email address, date, venue, type of shooting, how you heard about us and your message,
      and optionally your partner's name and phone number. We
      use this data only to answer your inquiry and, if it leads to a booking, to prepare and
      carry out the contract.
    </p>
    <p>
      The legal basis is the performance of pre-contractual measures at your request (Art. 6(1)(b)
      GDPR) and your consent given via the checkbox (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR). You can withdraw your
      consent at any time with effect for the future.
    </p>
    <p>
      The form content is not stored on the web server. It is sent directly as an email to our
      mailbox, which is hosted by Hostinger. We keep inquiries that do not lead to a booking for
      up to 12 months and then delete them. If a contract is concluded, statutory retention
      periods apply (in particular 7 years under § 132 BAO for accounting records).
    </p>

    <h2>5. Photos on this website</h2>
    <p>
      The galleries show people we have photographed. Photos are published only with the consent
      of the people shown. If you appear in a photo and want it removed, please contact us and we
      will remove it promptly.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>access your personal data (Art. 15)</li>
      <li>rectification of incorrect data (Art. 16)</li>
      <li>erasure (Art. 17)</li>
      <li>restriction of processing (Art. 18)</li>
      <li>data portability (Art. 20)</li>
      <li>object to processing based on legitimate interests (Art. 21)</li>
      <li>withdraw your consent at any time (Art. 7(3))</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To exercise your rights, write to <a href={`mailto:${legal.email}`}>{legal.email}</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you believe that the processing of your data violates data protection law, you can lodge
      a complaint with the Austrian Data Protection Authority (Österreichische
      Datenschutzbehörde), Barichgasse 40–42, 1030 Vienna,{' '}
      <a href="https://www.dsb.gv.at" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.dsb.gv.at</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Encryption</h2>
    <p>
      This website uses TLS encryption (HTTPS). You can recognise an encrypted connection by the
      lock symbol in your browser's address bar.
    </p>

    <p class="updated">Last updated: {legal.lastUpdated}</p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .updated {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
